  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Magnesium levulinate and Apolipoprotein B receptor, mediated through Selgantolimod. This relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, each indicating that Magnesium levulinate targets different entities—Keratin, Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A, and Plasma kallikrein—which are all targets of Selgantolimod. These targets are ultimately linked to the Apolipoprotein B receptor, suggesting a broader biological network involving Selgantolimod as a central mediator. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.7073) indicate a strong level of confidence in the observed relationships, though the exact mechanism by which Selgantolimod influences the Apolipoprotein B receptor remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence highlights the role of Selgantolimod as a bridge between Magnesium levulinate and the Apolipoprotein B receptor, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
